    <subfield code="a">Introduction / Don Snider -- Preface -- History of the camping movement -- The philosophy of the camping program -- Types of camps -- Administration -- The camp day -- Elements in the camp program -- Camping in the future -- Resources for the camp program -- Appendix. Application blank for camp leaders -- Sample enrollment card -- Health history for camp -- Approval of parents or guardians and waiver of claims -- Bibliography.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Let's Go Camping contains an analysis of the camping movement in the Church of the Brethren with many helpful suggestions on program planning and general management. The philosophy of the camp experience is skillfully and helpfully interpreted. - Introduction. The manual is designed to help the inexperienced camp leader. It is my hope that it will provide our leaders, many of whom serve in only one camp a year, an opportunity to understand the basic philsophy of the camp program and the techniques of camp leadership. Those who have had extended camping experience will not find many new ideas but will have an opportunity to review my philosophy of camping. - Preface.</subfield>
